>>>>> On Fri, 21 May 93 15:05:44 GMT, hafting@Lise.Unit.NO (Helge
>>>>> Hafting) said:

Helge> One charge for every 5-10 items (depending on cursed/blessed
Helge> status of wand) would be better.  This wand is supposed to be
Helge> powerful, don't cripple it too much.  The probabilities for
Helge> getting golems could be higher, so if you polumorph a huge pile
Helge> you should risk getting a golem for each n objects in the pile.
Helge> And larger piles should give golems with more HP...

I like that!  The complete pile could be replaced by a Golem, the
larger the pile the more risky it is to polymorph it.

Per> - Let intrinsic protections have a (long) time-out.

Helge> Not all of them!  What if your fire protection times out in Gehennom?
Helge> You would have to use up a ringfinger...

No no no.  Only intrinsic low armor class should time out, so a
contribution to a priest would only protect you for limited time.  The
larger the contribution, the more time the protection will work.  A
very large contribution may protect you for long enough to complete
the game.

Per> - Remove wands of wishing from the game.  Replace the wand with a
Per> magic lamp in the castle level. 

Helge> No!  

Hmm... I still think 5 wishes are too much.  How about having more
magic lamps, then?  Maybe in different miniquests?

Per> - Make it impossible to wish for named weapons.

Per> - Make it impossible to get a named weapon from the Gods.
 
Per> - Give the priest in Gehennom a named weapon, so the player have one
Per> in Hell.

Helge> It should at least be possible if you haven't seen one named
Helge> weapon yet.

I would like to reserve named weapon for the later stages of the game,
to make normal weapons interesting again.

Per> - Make intelligent monsters immune to conflict.

Helge> Not completely immune.  For each monster move, there could be a
Helge> chance for conflict to work, which is reduced with higher
Helge> intelligence.

I like this better.  Does monsters have an intelligence attribute?
 
Per> - Restrict wand zapping to high-level monsters, especially the more
Per> deadly wands.  A Gnome Lord should be allowed to zap magic missiles.

Helge> Death and sleep could be restricted, the others not.

Maybe what wands could be used should be determined by the monsters
intelligence attribute?

Per> - Make being killed when polymorphed lower your CON attribute, and if
Per> it is too low (< 5) you die for real.

Helge> I never understood why you should revert to human when killed
Helge> when polymorphed.  You should simply die.

Maybe because low level characters cannot protect themselves from
polymorph traps.  

Per> - A chrysknife should be significantly better than all other
Per> non-named weapons.

Helge> It seems unrealistic.

Yes, but the chrysknife is the only ordinary weapon with a mini-quest
associated, players should have some reward for solving that quest.
Also, if the chrysknife is made stronger the `need' for named weapon
would be less.

Per> - Players should be forced to drop all items that do not fit the
Per> players character class when entering the endgame.

Helge> Why?

It would make the endgame a lot more challenging, and it make sense
that players are true to there class when they are going to see their
God.  Like some deeply religious people (of any religion) chose to
abstain from the benefits of modern civilization.


